  "card": "Example, not reviewed library data. This record is not yet fully human-reviewed and may change in a later commit.\n\nLiquid water at 0.101325 MPa: density and dynamic viscosity at 293.15 K and 310.15 K, each field holding the two temperatures as alternatives (record_format.md section 5). The values are evaluated from the IAPWS formulations, R6-95(2018) for density and R12-08 for viscosity, and rounded to 6 significant digits. The pressure is an input of each evaluation: schema 0.1.0 has no pressure condition.\n\nThe uncertainties, as the releases state them. Density: a tolerance of 0.0001 % (R6-95(2018) section 6, p. 6, and Fig. 1, p. 16), to which no statistical significance can be attached, so it is not recorded as an uncertainty. Viscosity: 0.17 % at 293.15 K (R12-08 section 2.5, p. 4) and 1 % at 310.15 K (R12-08 Fig. 1, p. 4, read from the graphic), each recorded as a relative uncertainty with a coverage factor of two, as section 2.5 says of the figure's values. The viscosity formulation states no shear rate.",
